"""Plane project management platform manifest.

Open-source Jira / Linear alternative for tracking issues, sprints,
modules, roadmaps, pages, and analytics.

Architecture reference: https://github.com/makeplane/plane/blob/preview/docker-compose.yml
Source: https://github.com/makeplane/plane
"""

from scryr import Diagram, Info, Link, Manifest
from scryr.types import (
    Classification,
    DeploymentTarget,
    IncrementalVersion,
    Markdown,
    MetricTool,
    ProgrammingLanguage,
    Url,
    WebFramework,
    parse_version,
)

_SOURCE = Url("https://github.com/makeplane/plane")
_DOCS = Url("https://developers.plane.so/")
postgres_block = Manifest(
    name="PostgreSQL",
    icon="🐘",
    classification=Classification.database,
    tags=["database", "sql", "infra"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Project data model\n"
            "\n"
            "Primary relational database (postgres:15-alpine) storing all Plane data: workspaces, projects, issues, cycles, modules, pages, and members.\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Workspace boundary | Keep members and projects scoped to their workspace |\n"
            "| Issue history | Preserve relationships between issues, cycles, and modules |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Create an issue in a test workspace and move it into a cycle.\n"
            "2. Restore a test backup and inspect membership and issue associations.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** Schema changes can affect API requests and background workers at different times.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *query latency, lock contention, and connection pool usage*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "### Readiness checklist\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Exercise the happy path with test data.\n"
            "- [ ] Rehearse the failure and recovery path.\n"
            "- [ ] Record the owner, evidence, and follow-up in the deployment runbook.\n"
            "\n"
            "~~Assume a green process means the workflow works~~ — verify the end-to-end outcome as well.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - SQL clients for read-only inspection\n"
            "  - Query plans for index review\n"
            "  - Migration tooling for schema changes\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "  - `jaeger`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("15.7.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.sql],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.docker_swarm],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.grafana,
            MetricTool.loki,
            MetricTool.jaeger,
        ],
        links=[Link(site_name="Plane Docs", http_url=_DOCS)],
    ),
)
valkey_block = Manifest(
    name="Valkey",
    icon="🔴",
    classification=Classification.cache_store,
    tags=["cache", "celery", "infra"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Cache and task state\n"
            "\n"
            "Valkey 7 (Redis-compatible) used as both a cache layer and the Celery task broker for background workers and beat scheduler.\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Cache | Separate disposable responses from task-related state |\n"
            "| Expiry | Document which keys can be safely regenerated |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Invalidate a cached project response and reload it.\n"
            "2. Restart a test worker and inspect pending work before clearing any keys.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** Treating every key as disposable can remove task state as well as cached data.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *evictions, memory usage, and task backlog*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
