api_block = Manifest(
    name="API Server",
    icon="⚙️",
    classification=Classification.internal_api,
    tags=["api", "django", "core"],
    connections=[
        Manifest(name="PostgreSQL"),
        Manifest(name="Valkey"),
        Manifest(name="RabbitMQ"),
        Manifest(name="MinIO"),
    ],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Workspace API boundary\n"
            "\n"
            "Django REST Framework API server — the core backend of Plane. Handles authentication (magic-link, OAuth2, SAML), workspace and project management, issues, cycles, modules, views, analytics, webhooks, and Prisma-free direct PostgreSQL access via Django ORM.\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Authorization | Check membership for every workspace-scoped action |\n"
            "| Persistence | Commit issue changes before dispatching dependent tasks |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Create and update an issue through an authorized test client.\n"
            "2. Repeat the request using a user from another workspace.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** A valid user session alone does not grant access to every project.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *request errors, database latency, and task publication failures*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
